      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Xorphanol is a new mixed agonist-antagonist from the morphinan class of analgesics. On the basis of animal experiments, the physical dependence liability of xorphanol is predicted to be of a low order in man. Conceptually, xorphanol is of interest since in vitro experiments have revealed anti-naloxone properties and resistance to antagonism by opioid antagonists. At the practical level, xorphanol is a well tolerated, orally active analgesic that provides effective pain relief clinically."},
